14-Wolff3"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wolff</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name><name><surname>Roberts</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Mountjoy</surname><given-names>KG</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Physiological consequences of ectopic agouti gene expression: the yellow obese mouse syndrome.</article-title><source>Physiol Genomics</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>151</fpage><lpage>163</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11015573</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005414-Morgan1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Morgan</surname><given-names>HD</given-names></name><name><surname>Sutherland</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>DI</given-names></name><name><surname>Whitelaw</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Epigenetic inheritance at the agouti locus in the mouse.</article-title><source>Nat Genet</source><volume>23</volume><fpage>314</fpage><lpage>318</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10545949</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005414-Cooney1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cooney</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Dave</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolff</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Maternal methyl supplements in mice affect epigenetic variation and DNA methylation of offspring.</article-title><source>J Nutr</source><volume>132</volume><fpage>2393S</fpage><lpage>2400S</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12163699</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005414-Waterland1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-g